t tumor predisposition disorder caused by pathogenic variants in the MAX gene, characterized by an increased risk of pheochromocytoma and paraganglioma.\" [https://www.clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/hereditary-cancer/, PMID:20301715]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028020\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"MAX-related tumor predisposition\" EXACT [https://www.clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/hereditary-cancer/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nxref: GARD:0028020 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0008233 {source=\"OMIM:171300\"} ! pheochromocytoma\nis_a: MONDO:0017366 {source=\"PMID:20301715\", source=\"https://www.clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/hereditary-cancer/\"} ! hereditary pheochromocytoma-paraganglioma\nintersection_of: MONDO:0015356 ! hereditary neoplastic syndrome\nintersection_of: has_characteristic HP:0000006 ! Autosomal dominant inheritance\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/6913 ! MAX\nrelationship: has_characteristic HP:0000006 {source=\"OMIM:171300\", source=\"https://www.clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/hereditary-cancer/\"} ! Autosomal dominant inheritance\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9178\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0700347\nname: SDHC-related Mitochondrial Disease\ndef: \"Mitochondrial complex II deficiency due to pathogenic variants in the SDHC gene, resulting in a variety of clinical manifestations, including neurological and muscular symptoms.\" [https://www.clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/hereditary-cancer/]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028021\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"SDHC-related Mitochondrial Disease\" EXACT [https://www.clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/hereditary-cancer/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-regis