[Term]\nid: MONDO:0700375\nname: CDHR1-related retinopathy\ndef: \"Any retinopathy caused by variants in the CDHR1 gene, including cases diagnosed as cone-rod dystrophy 15, retinal macular dystrophy, or retinitis pigmentosa 65.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/ocular-cdwg/]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028030\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"CDHR1-related retinopathy\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/ocular-cdwg/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nxref: GARD:0028030 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0019118 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/ocular-cdwg/\"} ! inherited retinal dystrophy\nintersection_of: MONDO:0019118 ! inherited retinal dystrophy\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/14550 ! CDHR1\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/14550 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/ocular-cdwg/\"} ! CDHR1\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8986\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0700376\nname: GUCA1A-related retinopathy\ndef: \"Any retinopathy caused by a variant in the GUCA1A gene, including cases diagnosed as cone dystrophy 3 or cone-rod dystrophy 14.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/ocular-cdwg/]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028031\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"GUCA1A-related retinopathy\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/ocular-cdwg/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nxref: GARD:0028031 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0019118 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/ocular-cdwg/\"} ! inherited retinal dystrophy\nintersection_of: MONDO:0019118 ! inherited retinal dystrophy\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/4678 ! GUCA1A\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/4678 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/ocular-cdwg/\"} ! GUCA1A\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8986\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0700377\nname: NDP-related vitreoretinopathy\ndef: \"Any vitreoretinopathy caused by a variant in the NDP gene, including cases diagnosed as Norrie disease or X-linked exudative vitreoretinopathy 2.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/ocular-cdwg/]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028032\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"NDP-related vitreoretinopathy including Norrie syndrome\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/ocular-cdwg/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nxref: GARD:0028032 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0020246 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/ocular-cdwg/\"} ! inherited vitreoretinopathy\nintersection_of: MONDO:0020246 ! inherited vitreoretinopathy\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/7678 ! NDP\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/7678 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/ocular-cdwg/\"} ! NDP\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8986\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0700378\nname: WDPCP-related ciliopathy\ndef: \"Any ciliopathy caused by variants in the WDPCP gene, including cases diagnosed as Bardet-Biedl syndrome 15 or congenital heart defects, hamartomas of tongue, and polysyndactyly.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/ocular-cdwg/]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028033\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"WDPCP-related ciliopathy\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/ocular-cdwg/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nxref: GARD:0028033 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0005308 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/ocular-cdwg/\"} ! ciliopathy\nintersection_of: MONDO:0005308 ! ciliopathy\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/28027 ! WDPCP\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/28027 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/ocular-cdwg/\"} ! WDPCP\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8986\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0700379\nname: SDCCAG8-related ciliopathy\ndef: \"Any ciliopathy caused by variants in the SDCCAG8 gene, including cases diagnosed as Bardet-Biedl syndrome 16 or Senior-Loken syndrome 7.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/ocular-cdwg/]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028034\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"SDCCAG8-related ciliopathy\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/ocular-cdwg/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nxref: GARD:0028034 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0005308 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/ocular-cdwg/\"} ! ciliopathy\nintersection_of: MONDO:0005308 ! ciliopathy\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/10671 ! SDCCAG8\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/10671 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/ocular-cdwg/\"} ! SDCCAG8\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8986\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0700380\nname: RHO-related retinopathy\ndef: \"Any retinopathy caused by a variant in the RHO gene, including cases diagnosed as congenital stationary night blindness autosomal dominant 1 or retinitis pigmentosa 4.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/ocular-cdwg/]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028035\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"RHO-related retinopathy\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/ocular-cdwg/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nxref: GARD:0028035 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0019118 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/ocular-cdwg/\"} ! inherited retinal dystrophy\nintersection_of: MONDO:0019118 ! inherited retinal dystrophy\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/10012 ! RHO\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/10012 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/ocular-cdwg/\"} ! RHO\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8986\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0700382\nname: HMBS-related hepatic porphyria\ndef: \"A hepatic porphyria caused by monoallelic and biallelic variants in HMBS and presenting as a spectrum of disease (a semidominant inheritance pattern). Monoallelic variants predispose to acute/episodic attacks in adulthood with abdominal pain, neuropathy, and neuropsychiatric symptoms (women are more often affected) without cutaneous manifestations. Triggers precipitating acute attacks include estrogen/progesterone, oral contraceptives, alcohol, drugs, stress, or infections. Biallelic variants cause severe disease in childhood presenting with neurological issues including developmental abnormalities, ataxia, dysarthria, leukoencephalopathy, cataracts and optic nerve hypoplasia.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40097/]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028037\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"HMBS-related hepatic porphyria\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40097/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nxref: GARD:0028037 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0002520 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40097/\"} ! hepatic porphyria\nintersection_of: MONDO:0002520 ! hepatic porphyria\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/4982 ! HMBS\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9703\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0700383\nname: PPOX-related hepatic porphyria\ndef: \"A hepatic porphyria (or variegate porphyria) caused by monoallelic and biallelic variants in PPOX, presenting as a spectrum of disease (a semidominant inheritance pattern). Cases caused by monoallelic variants may have onset during adolescence or adulthood and are episodic characterized by abdominal pain, constipation, vomiting, muscular paralysis, and psychosis. Other symptoms may include abnormal blistering of the skin, cutaneous photosensitivity, and neuropathy. Triggers precipitating acute attacks include estrogen/progesterone, oral contraceptives, alcohol, drugs, stress, or infections. Cases caused by biallelic variants, which reduce enzyme activity to <25% of normal, typically result in child or adolescent onset with greater severity. Symptoms for this extend to brachydactyly, clinodactyly, intellectual disability, nystagmus, myopia, growth retardation, and hyperpigmentation.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40097/]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028038\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"PPOX-related hepatic porphyria\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40097/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nxref: GARD:0028038 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0002520 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40097/\"} ! hepatic porphyria\nintersection_of: MONDO:0002520 ! hepatic porphyria\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/9280 ! PPOX\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9703\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:0800026\nname: central hypoventilation syndrome, congenital, 1, with or without Hirschsprung disease\ndef: \"A rare disease due to a severely impaired central autonomic control of breathing and dysfunction of the autonomous nervous system. The incidence is estimated to be at 1 of 200 000 livebirths. A heterozygous mutation of PHOX-2B gene is found in 90% of the patients. Association with a Hirschsprung's disease is observed in 16% of the cases. Despite a high mortality rate and a lifelong dependence to mechanical ventilation, the long-term outcome of CCHS should be ultimately improved by multidisciplinary and coordinated follow-up of the patients.\" [Orphanet:661]\nsubset: clingen {source=\"MONDO:CLINGEN\"}\nsubset: doid {source=\"DOID:0060731\"}\nsubset: doid_rare {source=\"DOID:0060731\"}\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0008535\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: ncit {source=\"NCIT:C98889\"}\nsubset: nord_rare {source=\"MONDO:NORD\"}\nsubset: omim {source=\"OMIM:209880\"}\nsubset: ordo_disorder {source=\"Orphanet:661\"}\nsubset: orphanet {source=\"Orphanet:661\"}\nsubset: orphanet_rare {source=\"Orphanet:661\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"autonomic control, congenital failure of\" EXACT [OMIM:209880]\nsynonym: \"CCHS\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [DOID:0060731, MONDO:Lexical, OMIM:209880, Orphanet:661]\nsynonym: \"CCHS with Hirschsprung disease\" RELATED []\nsynonym: \"central hypoventilation syndrome, congenital\" RELATED [MONDO:Lexical]\nsynonym: \"congenital central alveolar hypoventilation syndrome\" EXACT [DOID:0060731, Orphanet:661]\nsynonym: \"congenital central hypoventilation\" EXACT [NCIT:C98889]\nsynonym: \"congenital central hypoventilation syndrome\" EXACT 