ps://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8866\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060109\nname: PLEC-related muscular dystrophy-epidermolysis bullosa simplex spectrum disorder\ndef: \"A spectrum of disease associated with loss or disrupted function of the PLEC gene. These disorders primarily affect the skin and muscles, leading to a range of symptoms including skin blistering (EBS), progressive muscle weakness (muscular dystrophy), and other complications.\" [PMID:35815343]\nsynonym: \"PLEC-related muscular dystrophy-epidermolysis bullosa simplex spectrum disorder\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2078-7280, PMID:35815343] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nsynonym: \"qualitative or quantitative defects of plectin\" NARROW []\nis_a: MONDO:0003847 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153\"} ! hereditary disease\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/9069 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2078-7280\"} ! PLEC\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8951\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060110\nname: HDAC4-related haploinsufficiency syndrome\ndef: \"A disorder caused by haploinsufficiency of HDAC4 and is characterized by brachydactyly type E, variable mild to moderate intellectual disability, seizures, autism spectrum disorder, short stature, obesity, and facial dysmorphism. Individuals with the gain of functions variants typically do not have brachydactyly and do have more consistent intellectual disability.\" [https://www.clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/, PMID:33537682]\ncomment: This term is more specific because it includes brachydactyly that is not characterized in the parent term. https://www.clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/\nsynonym: \"brachydactyly intellectual disability syndrome\" BROAD [https://www.clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/]\nsynonym: \"brachydactyly mental retardation syndrome\" BROAD DEPRECATED [https://www.clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/]\nsynonym: \"HDAC4-related haploinsufficiency syndrome\" EXACT [https://www.clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/, PMID:33537682] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0859232 {source=\"https://www.clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder with central hypotonia and dysmorphic facies\nrelationship: excluded_from_qc_check http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/mondo/sparql/qc/general/qc-single-child.sparql\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8897\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060111\nname: SAMD9L-related spectrum and myeloid neoplasm risk\ndef: \"A susceptibility or predisposition to myeloid neoplasms in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the SAMD9L gene. This condition is characterized by variable presentations of ataxia and cytopenia, myelodysplastic syndrome, monosomy 7 (acute myelogenous leukemia), and bone marrow failure.\" [MONDO:patterns/susceptibility_by_gene, PMID:29535429]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028150\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"SAMD9L-related spectrum and myeloid neoplasm risk\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/, https://orcid.org/0009-0004-3069-7846] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nxref: GARD:0028150 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0020573 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! inherited disease susceptibility\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/1349 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! SAMD9L\nrelationship: predisposes_towards MONDO:0008038 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! ataxia-pancytopenia syndrome\nrelationship: predisposes_towards MONDO:0018881 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! myelodysplastic syndrome\nrelationship: predisposes_towards MONDO:0044645 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! familial monosomy 7 syndrome\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8947\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060115\nname: TUBB4B-related ciliopathy\ndef: \"Any ciliopathy in which the cause of the disease is a variant in the TUBB4B gene. Please note that patient diagnoses can include disorders such as Leber congenital amaurosis and/or primary ciliary dyskinesia.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40102/]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028151\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"TUBB4B-related ciliopathy\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40102/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nxref: GARD:0028151 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0005308 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40102/\"} ! ciliopathy\nintersection_of: MONDO:0005308 ! ciliopathy\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/20771 ! TUBB4B\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/20771 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40102/\"} ! TUBB4B\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9001\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060120\nname: ACO2-related optic atrophy with or without extraocular features\ndef: \"An optic atrophy in which the cause of the disease is monoallelic or biallelic variants in the ACO2 gene. ACO2 is a mitochondrial protein and thus, in addition to the optic atrophy features, features of this disease include abnormal mitochondrial morphology and can affect other organ systems. Extraocular features can include ataxia, spastic paraplegia, CNS abnormalities, neurodevelopmental phenotypes, and retinal degeneration.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40077/, PMID:29564393]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028153\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"ACO2-related optic atrophy with or without extraocular features\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40077/, PMID:29564393] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nsynonym: \"infantile cerebellar-retinal degeneration\" RELATED [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40077/]\nsynonym: \"optic atrophy 9\" NARROW [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40077/]\nxref: GARD:0028153 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0003608 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40077/\"} ! optic atrophy\nis_a: MONDO:0044970 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40077/\"} ! mitochondrial disease\nintersection_of: MONDO:0003608 ! optic atrophy\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/118 ! ACO2\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/118 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40077/\"} ! ACO2\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9051\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060122\nname: ALG8-related autosomal dominant polycystic kidney and/or liver disease\ndef: \"An autosomal dominant disease caused by variants in the ALG8 gene that is characterized by incomplete penetrance and a range of clinical manifestations, spanning from individuals with normal kidneys to those with numerous kidney cysts and chronic kidney disease (CKD). While the common presentation involves a limited number of kidney cysts and maintained kidney function, severe polycystic liver disease (PLD) with minimal kidney involvement (ADPLD) can also occur.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40066/, PMID:39899384]\nsynonym: \"ADPKLD-ALG8\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40066/, PMID:39899384]\nsynonym: \"autosomal dominant polycystic kidney and/or liver disease-ALG8\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40066/, PMID:39899384] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0000426 {source=\"PMID:39899384\"} ! autosomal dominant disease\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/23161 {source=\"PMID:39899384\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40066/\"} ! ALG8\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9010\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060146\nname: FGFR1-related Pfeiffer syndrome\ndef: \"Any Pfeiffer syndrome in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the FGFR1 gene.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40059/, PMID:10861678, PMID:14564217, PMID:16957473, PMID:25251565, PMID:7874169]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028163\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"FGFR1-related Pfeiffer syndrome\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40059/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nxref: GARD:0028163 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0007043 {source=\"PMID:14564217\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40059/\"} ! Pfeiffer syndrome\nintersection_of: MONDO:0007043 ! Pfeiffer syndrome\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/3688 ! FGFR1\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/3688 {source=\"PMID:14564217\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40059/\"} ! FGFR1\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9155\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060147\nname: FGFR2-related Pfeiffer syndrome\ndef: \"Any Pfeiffer syndrome in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the FGFR2 gene.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40059/, PMID:15996217, PMID:7719333, PMID:7719345, PMID:9150725, PMID:9475590]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028164\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"FGFR2-related Pfeiffer syndrome\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40059/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nxref: GARD:0028164 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0007043 {source=\"PMID:9150725\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40059/\"} ! Pfeiffer syndrome\nintersection_of: MONDO:0007043 ! Pfeiffer syndrome\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/3689 ! FGFR2\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/3689 {source=\"PMID:9150725\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40059/\"} ! FGFR2\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9161\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060159\nname: complex movement disorder with or without neurodevelopmental features\ndef: \"A movement disorder characterized by having one or more different types of movement disorders, such as abnormal muscle tone, abnormal degree of movement, dystonia or torsion, which may occur with or without neurodevelopmental features, such as developmental delay or intellectual disability.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40113/]\nsynonym: \"complex movement disorder with or without neurodevelopmental features\" EXACT [] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0005395 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40113/\"} ! movement disorder\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9392\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060169\nname: HAVCR2-related cancer predisposition\ndef: \"Hereditary cancer predisposition due to variation(s) in the HAVCR2 gene, which confers the predisposition to susceptibility to subcutaneous panniculitis-like T-cell lymphoma (SPTCL) and hemophagocytic lymphohistiocytosis (HLH). Affected individuals typically present with multiple subcutaneous nodules and systemic B symptoms.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028172\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"HAVCR2-related SPTCL and/or HLH predisposition\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/]\nsynonym: \"HAVCR2-related subcutaneous panniculitis-like T-cell lymphoma and/or hemophagocytic lymphohistiocytosis predisposition\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nxref: GARD:0028172 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0015356 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! hereditary neoplastic syndrome\nintersection_of: MONDO:0015356 ! hereditary neoplastic syndrome\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/18437 ! HAVCR2\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/18437 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! HAVCR2\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9422\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060172\nname: FAM111A-related skeletal dysplasia\ndef: \"Any skeletal dysplasia in which the cause of the disease is a variation in FAM111A gene.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40106/, MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene, PMID:23684011, PMID:28138333, PMID:33263187, PMID:33750016, PMID:35205306, PMID:36916904, PMID:38679371, PMID:39501122]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028174\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"FAM111A-related skeletal dysplasia\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40106/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nxref: GARD:0028174 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0018230 {source=\"PMID:23684011\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40106/\"} ! skeletal dysplasia\nintersection_of: MONDO:0018230 ! skeletal dysplasia\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/24725 ! FAM111A\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/24725 {source=\"PMID:23684011\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40106/\"} ! FAM111A\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9527\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060173\nname: FLNB-associated autosomal dominant filamin related bone disorder\ndef: \"Any autosomal dominant filamin related bone disorder in which the cause of the disease is a variation in FLNB gene.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40106/, MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene, PMID:16752402, PMID:16801345, PMID:22190451, PMID:22354125]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028175\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"FLNB-associated autosomal dominant filamin related bone disorder\" EXACT [ht