PCCA\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/8653 {source=\"PMID:22593918\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/50162/\"} ! PCCA\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9662\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060183\nname: PCCB-related propionic acidemia\ndef: \"Any propionic acidemia in which the cause of the disease is a variation in PCCB gene.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/50162/, MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene, PMID:22593918]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028182\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"PCCB-related propionic acidemia\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/50162/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nxref: GARD:0028182 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0011628 {source=\"PMID:22593918\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/50162/\"} ! propionic acidemia\nintersection_of: MONDO:0011628 ! propionic acidemia\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/8654 ! PCCB\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/8654 {source=\"PMID:22593918\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/50162/\"} ! PCCB\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9662\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060184\nname: EGLN1-related erythrocytosis and pheochromocytoma/paraganglioma predisposition\ndef: \"Hereditary cancer predisposition due to variation(s) in the EGLN12 gene, which confers a predisposition to erythrocytosis and pheochromocytoma/paraganglioma.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028183\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"EGLN1-related erythrocytosis and pheochromocytoma/paraganglioma predisposition\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nxref: GARD:0028183 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0015356 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! hereditary neoplastic syndrome\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/1232 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! EGLN1\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9665\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060185\nname: systemic lupus erythematosus 18\ndef: \"Any systemic lupus erythematosus in which the cause of the disease is a variation in the PLD4 gene.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40123/, https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1738-6117, MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene, OMIM:621369]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028184\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: omim {source=\"OMIM:621369\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"SLEB18\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [OMIM:621369]\nsynonym: \"systemic lupus erythematosus related to PLD4\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40123/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nxref: GARD:0028184 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nxref: OMIM:621369 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0007915 {source=\"OMIM:621369\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40123/\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1738-6117\"} ! systemic lupus erythematosus\nintersection_of: MONDO:0007915 ! systemic lupus erythematosus\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/23792 ! PLD4\nrelationship: excluded_from_qc_check http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/mondo/sparql/qc/mondo/qc-omim-subsumption.sparql\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/23792 {source=\"OMIM:621369\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40123/\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1738-6117\"} ! PLD4\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9683\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060190\nname: APP-related brain and vascular amyloidosis\ndef: \"A hereditary amyloidosis characterized by a spectrum of neurodegenerative and neurovascular phenotypes caused by pathogenic variant in the APP gene, resulting in an abnormal clearance of amyloid peptides, either by overproduction and decreased clearance of amyloid peptides, with deposition of amyloid in plaques and blood vessel walls. Affected individuals may present with progressive cognitive decline, cerebral vascular amyloidosis with white matter changes, and stroke with or without hemorrhage.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40156/]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028185\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"APP-related brain and vascular amyloidosis\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40156/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nxref: GARD:0028185 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0011057 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40156/\"} ! cerebrovascular disorder\nis_a: MONDO:0018634 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40156/\"} ! hereditary amyloidosis\nis_a: MONDO:0024237 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40156/\"} ! inherited neurodegenerative disorder\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/620 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40156/\"} ! APP\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9721\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060191\nname: ciliopathy-IFT74\ndef: \"Any ciliopathy caused by variants in the IFT74 gene.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40066, PMID:27486776, PMID:33531668, PMID:33748949, PMID:34539760, PMID:37315079, PMID:37555648]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028186\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"ciliopathy-IFT74\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40066] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nxref: GARD:0028186 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0005308 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40066\"} ! ciliopathy\nintersection_of: MONDO:0005308 ! ciliopathy\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/21424 ! IFT74\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/21424 {source=\"PMID:37555648\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40066\"} ! IFT74\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9732\" xsd:string\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060194\nname: FAS-related autoimmune lymphoproliferative syndrome\ndef: \"An autoimmune lymphoproliferative syndrome that results from defective lymphocyte homoestasis, and is caused by variants in the FAS gene. It is characterized by non-malignant lymphoproliferation, autoimmune disease, and lifelong increased risk for both Hodgkin and non-Hodgkin lymphoma.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028187\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"FAS-related autoimmune lymphoproliferative syndrome\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nxref: GARD:0028187 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0017979 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! autoimmune lymphoproliferative syndrome\nintersection_of: MONDO:0017979 ! autoimmune lymphoproliferative syndrome\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/11920 ! FAS\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/11920 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! FAS\nrelationship: predisposes_towards MONDO:0004952 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! Hodgkins lymphoma\nrelationship: predisposes_towards MONDO:0018908 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! non-Hodgkin lymphoma\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9749\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060195\nname: SH2B3-related immune system disorder\ndef: \"A predisposition caused by a mutation in SH2B3 gene that presents with myeloproliferation and/or multi-organ autoimmunity.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/]\nsynonym: \"SH2B3-related immune system disorder\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nsynonym: \"SH2B3-related myeloproliferation and autoimmunity\" RELATED [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/]\nis_a: MONDO:0020573 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! inherited disease susceptibility\nintersection_of: MONDO:0020573 ! inherited disease susceptibility\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/29605 ! SH2B3\nintersection_of: predisposes_towards MONDO:0005046 ! immune system disorder\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/29605 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! SH2B3\nrelationship: predisposes_towards MONDO:0005046 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! immune system disorder\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9576\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060197\nname: congenital heart disease with heterotaxy syndrome\ndef: \"A heart disease that is present at birth that occurs with variable extracardiac laterality defects. Features of visceral heterotaxy are not always present but can include abnormal location of the organs within the thoracic, abdominal, or peritoneal cavities. Anatomic and functional problems can include intestinal malrotation leading to volvulus, biliary atresia, and various defects of the central nervous system, urinary tract, and skeleton.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40130/, PMID:19064609, PMID:30293987, PMID:34666056]\nsynonym: \"congenital heart disease with heterotaxy syndrome\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40130/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40130/\"} ! syndromic disease\nis_a: MONDO:0005453 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40130/\"} ! congenital heart disease\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9463\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060211\nname: NR5A1-related sex development disorder\ndef: \"A reproductive system disorder caused by a variation in the NR5A1 gene, and characterized by varying phenotypes, including partial or complete gonadal dysgenesis, ambiguous genitalia, and spermatogenic failure in the male, and premature ovarian failure and ovarian dysgenesis in the female.\" [https://www.clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40073/, PMID:28033660, PMID:31513305]\ncomment: 46XY individuals can present with azoospermia, hypospadias, micropenis, cryptorchidism, ambiguous or female-appearing genitalia, partial or complete gonadal dysgenesis, Sertoli dysfunction, and progressive testicular failure. Leydig function is often partially preserved, and infertility is common. 46XX individuals can present with primary ovarian insufficiency/ premature ovarian failure, ovarian dysgenesis, and subfertility. Rarely, testicular or ovotesticular disorder of sex development may occur. Individuals typically have normal adrenal function but in rare cases, adrenal insufficiency may be observed in the context of severe-early onset variants.\nsynonym: \"NR5A1-related sex development disorder\" EXACT [https://www.clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40073/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0005039 {source=\"PMID:28033660\", source=\"https://www.clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40073/\"} ! reproductive system disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0005039 ! reproductive system disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/7983 ! NR5A1\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/7983 {source=\"PMID:28033660\"} ! NR5A1\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9863\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060212\nname: CRYAB-related myofibrillar myopathy-cataract-cardiomyopathy spectrum disorder\ndef: \"A syndromic disease caused by a variation in the CRYAB gene, and characterized by a spectrum of phenotypes including cardiomyopathy, cataract, and/or myopathy.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2078-7280, PMID:21920752, PMID:38212463]\nsynonym: \"alpha-B crystallinopathy\" RELATED [PMID:21920752]\nsynonym: \"CRYAB-related myofibrillar myopathy-cataract-cardiomyopathy spectrum disorder\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2078-7280] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2078-7280\"} ! syndromic disease\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/2389 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2078-7280\"} ! CRYAB\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9774\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060214\nname: SYCE1-related gametogenic failure\ndef: \"An infertility disorder caused by variation in the SYCE1 gene. Affected males may present with non-obstructive azoospermia due to maturation arrest or meiotic failure, while affected females may present with primary ovarian insufficiency.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40073/, PMID:32402064, PMID:35718780]\nsynonym: \"SYCE1-related gametogenic failure\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40073/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0005047 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40073/\"} ! infertility disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0005047 ! infertility disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/28852 ! SYCE1\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/28852 {source=\"PMID:32402064\", source=\"PMID:35718780\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40073/\"} ! SYCE1\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9864\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:8000006\nname: WHIM syndrome 1\ndef: \"A congenital autosomal dominant immune deficiency characterized by abnormal retention of mature neutrophils in the bone marrow (myelokathexis) and occasional hypogammaglobulinemia, associated with an increased risk for bacterial infections and a susceptibility to human papillomavirus (HPV) induced lesions (cutaneous warts, genital dysplasia and invasive mucosal carcinoma).\" [Orphanet:51636]\nsubset: doid {source=\"DOID:0060591\"}\nsubset: doid_rare {source=\"DOID:0060591\"}\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0009297\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: nord_rare {source=\"NORD:1849\", source=\"MONDO:NORD\"}\nsubset: omim {source=\"OMIM:193670\"}\nsubset: ordo_disorder {source=\"Orphanet:51636\"}\nsubset: orphanet {source=\"Orphanet:51636\"}\nsubset: orphanet_rare {source=\"Orphanet:51636\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"myelokathexis, isolated\" EXACT []\nsynonym: \"Warts, hypogammaglobulinemia, infections, and myelokathexis syndrome\" EXACT []\nsynonym: \"Warts-hypogammaglobulinemia-infections-myelokathexis syndrome\" EXACT [DOID:0060591, Orphanet:51636]\nsynonym: \"Warts-infections-leukopenia-myelokatexis syndrome\" EXACT [Orphanet:51636]\nsynonym: \"WHIM Syndrome\" EXACT [NORD:1849, Orphanet:51636] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/nord\"}\nsynonym: \"WHIM syndrome\" BROAD [MONDO:Lexical]\nsynonym: \"WHIMS\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [DOID:0060591, MONDO:Lexical, OMIM:193670]\nsynonym: \"WILM\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [Orphanet:51636]\nxref: DOID:0060591 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: GARD:0009297 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nxref: ICD10CM:D81.8 {source=\"Orphanet:51636\", source=\"Orphanet:51636/attributed\", source=\"Orphanet:51636/ntbt\", source=\"DOID:0060591\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:1778124 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: MESH:C536697 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"Orphanet:51636\", source=\"Orphanet:51636/e\", source=\"DOID:0060591\"}\nxref: NORD:1849 {source=\"MONDO:NORD\"}\nxref: OMIM:193670 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"Orphanet:51636\", source=\"Orphanet:51636/e\", source=\"